WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.600
I'm gonna be the first-star idol one day!

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.650
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:15.070
It's hard to believe that it's already almost been half a year

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:18.330
since we entered Four Star Academy and started our Aikatsu.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:21.330
I wonder what we'll be doing this time next year. {S2, of course}

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.960
I'll make sure to be in S4 by then!

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.460
The same goes for me!

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:28.630
But what do we need to get there?

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.670
Maybe it's individuality.

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:35.300
Anna-sensei's always going on about "Individuality!" and all that.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.720
Hey, what do you think makes me unique?

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.980
Maybe your energy? {enthusiasm. also how mad would people get if I just used "genki"}{I think that's the scale people tend get less angry about}

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:45.440
That's so generic.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:48.650
You're lucky, Rola. You've got your whole "rock" thing.

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:50.980
I couldn't have found it without you.

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:54.360
Chin up, now it's your turn to find it.

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:58.120
All right! I'm gonna find out what my individuality is!

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:04.410
Hey, have you read all of these?

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:11.420
Books free me from my confines and lead me to lands of fantasy.

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:16.180
Lilienne, you're always so poetic! {her real name is Lily, this is Yuzu's nickname}

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:17.680
Here, for you.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:19.800
A ticket to your event?

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:26.060
Yep! I'm gonna be having a solo live at the plateau hotel right nearby.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:27.940
Are you, now?

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:31.320
And I wanted you to come watch.

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:35.450
The unkind rays of summer sun

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:41.280
have left the sky, driven out by the soft light of fall.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.450
I can feel the gentle touch of autumn.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:48.580
Allow me to partake in the viewing of your gallant display.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.090
Yay!

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.430
Four Star Academy's seven luckies? {here's the deal: it doesn't make sense in japanese either, and the seven things are objects, events, actions, and people}{it makes more sense in japanese because it could be seven anythings and parts of speech are a social construct}

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:33.810
Yeah! They say that your dream will come true if you can find them all.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:37.020
So they answer your prayers?

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:39.070
I think that's pretty close.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:45.070
All right! I'm gonna find all seven and wish for a strong sense of individuality!

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:46.330
I'm in!

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:50.710
Come on, investigation starts from the legs!

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:52.830
You're making a really big deal out of this.

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:56.460
So where should we start looking?

00:03:56.460 --> 00:04:02.630
The first says to search for four enormous aligned stars inside the school.

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:06.470
Then you will become a big star yourself.

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:09.560
It sounds like S4's emblem.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:10.770
I know that one.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:14.350
Mahiru-chan!

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:18.360
Those are definitely four big stars!

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:23.610
Thanks, Mahiru-chan! Hopefully we can find the rest just as easily.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:27.120
For the second, make a prayer to the infinite world. {so close to being able to use eternal world}

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:32.000
Declare your resolve to your infinite self within the mirror.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:35.920
Just a mirror? There're so many of those on campus.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:38.630
And what does it mean by "infinite self"?

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:40.880
It doesn't sound like an ordinary mirror.

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:54.020
Infinite world complete!

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:56.150
I'm gonna find my individuality!

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:57.770
Daily devotion!

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:59.770
Sharpen my singing!

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:02.570
I don't want to lose to Onee-chan!

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:08.530
Number three. If you desire flair, find the dancing fairy!

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:12.080
Found the fairy!

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:17.170
Number four. If you meet a beautiful person in the art room,

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:20.290
you yourself will become just as beautiful.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:27.510
I don't see any beauties, or anyone at all for that matter.

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:40.060
It's a beautiful person!

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:41.900
This is what it meant?

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:46.070
Please share some of your beauty!

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:51.330
Number five. To sharpen your dance moves, step to the rhythm of time.

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.330
It's gotta be this, right?

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:56.710
This is the only clock in the school that plays music.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:01.840
It's time!

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:17.100
Hey, quiet in the library! 
What are you even doing?

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:20.770
Please let us finish the dance!

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:27.610
Number six. After nightfall, open your ears to the melody of a tiny piano,

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:30.950
and say a charm to make your singing improve.

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:44.550
May my singing improve!

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:45.840
Improve!

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.380
Improve!

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:53.430
So we made it to the last one,

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:56.680
but where are we supposed to find it?

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:59.390
Unlike the other ones, we don't even know where to start.

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:00.690
It's a mystery.

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:06.070
Search for the Tundra Diva who turns all who look upon her to ice.

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:08.150
Where could she be hiding?

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:11.700
And anyway, what kind of person is a diva?

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.580
Hello! I'm Nikaidou Yuzu!

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:23.000
I'll be counting on you today!

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:26.090
Yuzu-chan! We're expecting great things for today's concert.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:30.590
Okay! I'll go full power, all-out today!

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:39.850
Cold! {aw shit, nega-Juri}

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:44.520
Yuzu.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:47.320
Lilienne, you came!

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:48.980
What a splendid day. {this and the following are actual quotes http://www.goodreads.com/quotes/tag/anne-of-green-gables}

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:52.990
Were it Anne of Green Gables, she would say,

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:56.990
"Isn't it good just to be alive on a day like this?"

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:01.250
I know you just got here, but can you help me stretch?

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:04.130
Sure, I would be glad to.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:09.130
One, two, three, four.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:12.630
Is something the matter?

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:17.510
I just remembered that we used to stretch like this back when we were kids too.

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:22.940
Hey, Lilienne. Can you help me stretch?

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:25.150
Sure, I would be glad to.

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:31.240
Ow, ow, ow!

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.150
I can't, I can't, I can't!

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:38.990
Were it Edison, he would say, 
"Our greatest weakness lies in giving up."{by the way you know that "thusly" was originally used to make fun of uneducated people who tried to speak fancy but failed}{not according to my research}

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:45.210
Such old memories.

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:48.290
Yuzu, you haven't changed a touch since those days.

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:51.550
Ow, ow, ow!

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:55.550
Man, Lilienne, you haven't changed at all either!

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:04.310
Yuzu had an aha moment!

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:09.440
What about?

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:23.580
We've been looking all day,

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:28.210
but we still haven't found a single lead on the seventh lucky, the Tundra Diva.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:31.500
Where could she be?

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:34.380
Also, what's a "tundra"?

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:37.010
Huh? You were looking without even knowing?

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:44.140
It refers to a region with a layer of 
permafrost that stays frozen year round. {I know it's not quite the real definition}

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:48.600
Does that mean we won't be able to find her until winter?

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:51.610
Do we even have someone like that on campus?

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:59.660
Either way, we managed to find the 
other six, so I'm willing to call this a win.

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:04.540
Well, I'm not! It won't work unless we find all seven.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.120
Are you giving up on finding your individuality?

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:09.920
Of course not!

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:11.630
Then stick with it.

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:16.380
Coming all this way and still not finding it only makes me want it more!

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:19.720
Giving up now feels the same as losing!

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:22.140
I'll find it at any cost!

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:29.020
What? You would offer me a place in the event?

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:33.440
Ding dong! The staff already gave me the green light.

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.530
Can we count on you?

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:40.160
Is that a no?

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:43.410
Are you not feeling better yet?

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:47.120
No, that is not the case.

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:50.290
I was simply not expecting this.

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:56.170
I didn't think I'd ever hear those words coming from your mouth.

00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:00.970
Don't you remember our elementary school arts festival?

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:04.430
Someone suddenly got sick the day of the main event,

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:08.930
but then you managed to play both your role and theirs!

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:13.810
And your part was even the princess!

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:17.480
Such a beautiful night this is.

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:20.570
I must prepare for the ball!

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:26.950
Then you stepped in to play the prince's friend!

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:29.330
The stars are so distant tonight.

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:32.880
Can you not feel the gears of fate turning?

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:36.170
You totally nailed it!

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:37.590
Yes.

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:40.670
So why do you look so anxious?

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:46.810
Were I to single out one source of my unease, it would be time.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:49.310
Time, you say?

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:53.440
Only scant sand remains in the hourglass.

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:58.530
Even the most beautiful jewels can scarcely glimmer when encrusted in earth.

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:05.490
It is only with time to polish that they shine brilliantly in the eyes of people.

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:08.160
So...

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:09.830
There's one of her proverbs!

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:10.580
What?

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:14.580
You're saying that there's not enough time until the show starts.

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:17.460
Fear not! I'll help you out!

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:20.460
But then your own performance would suffer.

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:27.100
Now, now. You know better than anyone else that I'm strongest when the chips are down.

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:30.100
That's true.

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:34.900
You're about to come back to school, so consider this a warm-up!

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:40.400
Excellent point. So long as an ounce of will remains, failure is nothing to fear.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:42.570
That is yet another saying.

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:44.240
Then it's decided!

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:47.450
Should we update the program and give it a run?

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:48.330
No.

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:54.750
Before that, may I have some time to focus my mind?

00:12:55.790 --> 00:13:00.130
I must summon the goddess from beyond the heavens!

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:04.130
Now that you're in, you're not holding anything back.

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:05.300
Yes.

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:07.890
A-All right.

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:10.260
Let us support one another.

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:19.520
Why can't we find it?

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:23.900
Show yourself already, Tundra Diva!

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:26.910
Why are you shouting like that?

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:29.910
Oh, Katsura-senpai, I'm so sorry.

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:34.040
Could it be that you're searching for the school's seven luckies?

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:35.660
Yes, we are.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:38.670
Doesn't that bring back memories, Katsura-senpai?

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:42.460
It sure does. Everyone goes through it at least once.

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:43.550
Yep.

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:46.130
So how many have you found?

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:47.550
Six so far.

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:52.010
Yeah, it's pretty easy going up until that point.

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:54.930
Right, right, everyone can clear the first few.

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:57.060
The problem is the seventh.

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:58.650
It's got us too.

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:02.690
We just can't figure out who the Tundra Diva is supposed to be.

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:05.780
Oh, I suppose that goes without saying.

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:08.200
The diva's on a break from school right now.

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:11.330
Huh? She's a real person who goes here?

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:16.500
Yep. And the seventh lucky changes every year.

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:20.670
Right, right! Can anyone figure out who the Stern Greek Sculpture is? {am I stupid? this said Greece. you messed up too eto}

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:25.590
Tsubasa-senpai?

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:26.840
Bingo!

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:28.340
I can see that!

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:32.220
So back to this year, the Tundra Diva it's talking about

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:35.970
is a second-year in Song Class, Shirogane Lily.

00:14:36.310 --> 00:14:39.230
Shirogane Lily-san.

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:43.520
She's an admin like me, but she has a frail constitution.

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:46.360
She spends this season recuperating at the plateau.

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:52.740
A frail constitution and lives at the plateau... so where's the tundra part come from?

00:14:52.740 --> 00:14:56.620
Well, it's actually quite difficult to explain it in words.

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:01.630
In any case, she's extremely individualistic!

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:05.750
She's so ridiculously unique that some may even call her a walking individuality!

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:09.380
Ridiculously unique? I'd like to meet her!

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:12.640
I believe she should be returning soon.

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:14.810
Then I can't see her right away.

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:19.390
Oh, but the reference section of the library should have video of her from last year.

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:25.020
These video files are it, right?

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:29.400
Shirogane Lily-san...

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:30.650
There, found her!

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:38.200
I just felt a shiver down my spine.

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:40.410
So this is the Tundra Diva...

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:43.420
Incredible...

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:49.300
Be-li-lieve it or not, we've got a surprise guest for you!{I see what you did or didn't do}{it just sounded nice, wasn't thinking of that other girl}

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:54.680
She's from Four Star Academy like me, so meet my friend...

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:57.060
Shirogane Lily-chan!

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:08.570
Wait, isn't that...

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:09.940
She's back!

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:13.450
Cold!

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:26.040
Birds tweet, flowers blossom, and even Saturn dances with joy, yet something is still missing. {the god, not the planet}{for what purpose would you remove that}

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:31.590
Yes—without song, people will forever be ignorant of love!

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:37.850
And without further ado, it's time for Lily-chan's performance!

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:45.480
Dark green reminiscent of an autumn lake

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:47.770
and the purple of a twilight sky.

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:52.740
Distinctive as a single flower blooming in the midst of a snowfield.

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:59.120
Shirogane Lily, pouring my soul into this moment!

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:20.780
Lily-chan, welcome back!

00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:24.030
Thank you very much.

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:31.910
Back and better than ever! Great job!

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:34.670
Here, it's your favorite.

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:36.750
Vienna coffee. {twice as many google results}

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:39.840
Are you okay?

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:43.550
Isn't it splendid there are so many things to like in this world? {also direct quote}

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:46.430
Is that a proverb?

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:51.520
It's one of Anne's lines that comes to mind whenever I sing.

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:53.890
It hasn't come in quite a while.

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:57.440
I am incredibly grateful that you gave me this opportunity.

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:00.940
You're very welcome!

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:05.820
Both the color and design of her dress.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:10.240
It's hard to put into words, but you can really feel her particularities. {NNO}

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:12.700
And her presence was something else.

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:15.460
That just makes me want to meet her more!

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:19.710
Katsura-senpai said she'd be returning to school soon.

00:21:19.710 --> 00:21:21.460
I wonder when exactly.

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:23.090
I can hardly wait!

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:27.090
We ended up finding all seven luckies,

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:30.350
but individuality is something you've gotta find yourself.

00:21:30.680 --> 00:21:31.560
Yeah.

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:32.930
That's true.

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:34.810
I've got it!

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:39.360
How about we start by coming up with catchphrases of our own? {Yume, no.}

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:41.480
Catchphrases?

00:21:41.820 --> 00:21:44.740
Don't you want something like the Tundra Diva?{.} {Yume, no. That's not a catchphrase.}

00:21:46.740 --> 00:21:53.500
I feel like having a firm grasp of your identity is the first step to individuality.

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:55.120
That gets me going! {thank you for the correct example}

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:56.540
I get it.

00:21:56.540 --> 00:21:58.000
You have a point.

00:21:58.380 --> 00:22:01.290
All right, then I'll be...

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:05.630
The Shining Glimmer... no, that's not it.

00:22:05.630 --> 00:22:08.130
Wait, wait, the Silver Snow...

00:22:08.680 --> 00:22:10.010
Why snow?

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:12.560
Then Above the Clouds...

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:15.020
Oh, the Messenger of Heaven!

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:17.890
Not quite... the Playful Fallen Angel.

00:22:17.890 --> 00:22:20.400
The Clever Cub. And next...

00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:23.780
Yume-chan's search for her individuality is far from over.

00:24:00.250 --> 00:24:05.500
I was really happy to see Lily take part in a serious performance after all this time.

00:24:06.090 --> 00:24:10.050
I applied plenty of stamps to celebrate her return.

00:24:10.420 --> 00:24:12.880
Yume, your family runs a confectionery, right?

00:24:12.880 --> 00:24:16.510
Cream puffs and shortcake, even chocolate brownies!

00:24:16.510 --> 00:24:18.770
No overeating, okay?

00:24:18.770 --> 00:24:20.480
Next time on Aikatsu Stars!

00:24:20.480 --> 00:24:22.060
